  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "線性控制系統(二)",
    "sub_ename": "LINEAR CONTROL SYSTEM(2)",
    "describe_ch": "本課程為控制系統領域之入門，並藉此培植學生具備控制系統工程師之養成智識。其內容涵蓋基礎的動力學系統之數學模型建構。各種模式(例如： Frequency-Domain) 之數學模型建構及分析，自動控制系統理論及電腦控制系統等。細部的重要理論包括：例如the Bode diagram, and state variable methods for simulation and control system design. 此外，目前在工業界控制領域中最為廣泛使用之電腦程式語言MATLAB，亦會於課程內容介紹，使學生了解如何使用MATLAB解決線性控制系統相關問題。",
    "describe_eh": "This course is the introductory course in control systems, and is intended to equip students with detailed familiarity with historically significant tools of the control engineer. Topics include the fundamentals of dynamics system modeling; modeling systems from various physical domains and systems; and an introduction to the concepts and theory pertinent to automatic control systems, including computer control systems. The course also covers a detailed discussion of the Bode diagram, and state variable methods for simulation and control system design. Besides, the most well-known programming language in control field industry, MATLAB, is also introduced to provide assistance in solving computational problems associated with the linear control systems.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 3.0
  },
  "targets": [
    {
      "seq": 1,
      "describe_ch": "了解Frequency Domain Analysis的特性與基本架構。",
      "describe_en": "To understand the feature and basic framework of Frequency Domain Analysis."
    },
    {
      "seq": 2,
      "describe_ch": "了解Nyquist Plot模型建構與Gain Margin, Phase Margin 之關聯性。",
      "describe_en": "To understand the Nyquist Plot, Gain Margin, Phase Margin, and their relationship."
    },
    {
      "seq": 3,
      "describe_ch": "熟悉Bode diagram之意義及建構與其應用。",
      "describe_en": "To construct and get familiar with Bode diagram and its application."
    },
    {
      "seq": 4,
      "describe_ch": "能應用課程所學之控制法則與圖形工具來分析判斷線性控制系統之穩定性。",
      "describe_en": "To be able to construct the control law and use diagrams learned from this course to analyze the stability of linear control systems."
    }
  ],
